WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.630
Lucía is telling a story:
Comía cuando sonó el teléfono.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.010
"I was eating when the phone rang.

3
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.970
" Two verbs, both in the
past, both in one sentence.

4
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.410
But they don't use
the same past tense.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.290
So how do you choose
which past to use?

6
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.250
In this mission, you'll put
the preterite and the imperfect

7
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.530
side by side and see
the job each one does.

8
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.690
You'll sort time phrases
by the tense they signal,

9
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.710
like ayer and todos los días.

10
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.570
And you'll spot when a
sentence is pure description.

11
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.050
Your mission: work out how to
choose between these two past

12
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.210
tenses.
